":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.5 master and 4.4.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.stable.mono - macOS Sequoia (15.3.2) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Metal (Mobile) - integrated Apple M4 Pro (Apple9) - Apple M4 Pro (12 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen attempting to use `CanvasItem` shader instance uniforms inside custom functions, there're tons of shader compilation error messages thrown out in the editor output, and instance uniforms do not work while parameters have appeared in the inspector.\nIt seems that this issue only occurs in RD based pipelines, on Compatibility everything works well.\n\n\n```glsl\nshader_type canvas_item;\n\ninstance uniform float test = 0.0f;\n\nfloat test_function(float x)\n{\n\treturn x * test;\n}\n\nvoid fragment() {\n\tCOLOR.rgb *= test_function(1.0);\n}\n```\n\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4c18e8af-9ce2-4dd9-9ac0-db6e082f43b5)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nOpen the MRP project, and see the output. Also sprites' color in the viewport won't be changed by their instance shader parameters.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[instance_uniform_mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19437208/instance_uniform_mrp.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"maidopi-usagi","id":33864304,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzODY0MzA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33864304?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maidopi-usagi","html_url":"https://github.com/maidopi-usagi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maidopi-usagi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maidopi-usagi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maidopi-usagi/gists